The code works with a 2D grid where each cell represents a pixel.
Index2D is used to represent a position in the grid using x and y coordinates.
Map stores the grid as a 2D array and provides methods to initialize the map, change pixel values, draw shapes, and perform flood fill using BFS.
Ex2_GUI displays the grid in a pixelized way, follows the mouse with a pink trail, and includes a blocked area in the center.
The JUnit tests verify the correctness of the map logic, while the GUI is used only for visualization.

Index2D
Constructor – creates a pixel with x and y coordinates
getX / getY – return the pixel coordinates
distance2D – calculates distance between two pixels
equals / hashCode – compare pixels by position

Map
init / constructors – create or reset the map
getMap / getWidth / getHeight – return map data and size
getPixel / setPixel – read or change a pixel value
isInside – checks if a pixel is inside the map
sameDimensions – checks if two maps have the same size
addMap2D / mul / rescale – modify the map values or size
drawLine / drawRect / drawCircle – draw shapes on the map
fill – fills connected pixels using BFS
shortestPath – finds the shortest path between two pixels
allDistance – calculates distances from a starting pixel
equals – checks if two maps are identical

Ex2_GUI
main – starts the GUI
pixelMouseWorld – runs the pixelized mouse-follow GUI
drawCell – draws one pixel on the screen
inside / inBlock / clamp – helper functions for bounds and limits

